    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## recv-wazuh-alert (contract C1, N8N-1.1, N8N-1.8)\n**Trigger:** POST /webhook/wazuh-alert from the Wazuh `custom-n8n` integration, header `X-ASOX-Token` required (403 without it, N8N-1.6). Answers 200 **after the alert is in the queue** (C1 has a 10 s timeout and no retries): a 200 means queued (or filtered). If n8n dies first, the delivery fails and Wazuh logs it.\n**Inputs:** raw Wazuh alert JSON (body). The full alert stays in this execution (the C1 check looks for it here).\n**Actions taken:** drops alerts below WAZUH_ALERT_MIN_LEVEL (\"filtered: level ...\", 200, no row); inserts every other alert, raw, into the n8n Data Table `asox_alert_queue` (N8N-1.4) and answers 200. **Nothing else runs before the insert: no Code node, no sub-workflow** (N8N-1.8: 20 deliveries at once got n8n OOM-killed while each ran lib-config, lib-route-alert and five Code nodes). Intake exclusions and routing happen in lib-alert-queue-drain, at most `alert_queue.slots` at once. If the queue is unavailable (insert refused), it answers 200 and then, as before the queue, reads lib-config, applies the intake exclusions, routes with lib-route-alert and calls the playbook by ID without waiting; a routing failure there parks the alert with its id through lib-error.\n**Systems changed:** none here (the playbooks change TheHive).\n**Approval:** not applicable.\n**Owner:** n8n.\nError workflow: recv-n8n-error.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 520
      },
